{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_011QCNaBd8t592eRfYDDnotK", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.amazon.com/Baptists-Jews-Holocaust-Sincere-Friendship/dp/0817017828\"}, {\"url\": \"https://books.google.com/books/about/Baptists_Jews_and_the_Holocaust.html?id=rsONswEACAAJ\"}, {\"url\": \"https://x.com/leespitzer\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.churchleadership.com/author/lee-b-spitzer/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.amazon.com/Sympathy-Solidarity-Silence-Responses-Holocaust/dp/0817018352\"}, {\"url\": \"https://baptistnews.com/article/baptists-enough-respond-holocaust-complicated-says-baptist-leader-new-book/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.judsonpress.com/Products/J253/baptists-jews-and-the-holocaust.aspx\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.baptistholocauststudies.org/about\"}, {\"url\": \"https://new.judsonpress.com/jp-3/lee-b-spitzer\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.baptistholocauststudies.org/news/2017/10/24/christian-citizen-publishes-holocaust-article\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:29:35.917Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Lee B. Spitzer author bio \"Baptists, Jews, and the Holocaust\" PhD in church history OR theology OR \"history of Christianity\" Vrije Universiteit", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01GLpPwai1iHFc8P14dLZhbF", "content": [{"title": "Baptists, Jews, and the Holocaust: The Hand of Sincere Friendship: Spitzer, Lee B, Trulson, Reid: 9780817017828: Amazon.com: Books", "url": "https://www.amazon.com/Baptists-Jews-Holocaust-Sincere-Friendship/dp/0817017828"}, {"title": "Baptists, Jews, and the Holocaust: The Hand of Sincere Friendship - Lee B. Spitzer - Google Books", "url": "https://books.google.com/books/about/Baptists_Jews_and_the_Holocaust.html?id=rsONswEACAAJ"}, {"title": "Rev. Dr. Lee B. Spitzer (@leespitzer) / Posts ...", "url": "https://x.com/leespitzer"}, {"title": "Lee B. Spitzer, Author at Lewis Center for Church Leadership", "url": "https://www.churchleadership.com/author/lee-b-spitzer/"}, {"title": "Sympathy, Solidarity, and Silence: Three European Baptist Responses to the Holocaust: Spitzer, Lee B: 9780817018351: Amazon.com: Books", "url": "https://www.amazon.com/Sympathy-Solidarity-Silence-Responses-Holocaust/dp/0817018352"}, {"title": "Did Baptists do enough to respond to the Holocaust? It’s complicated, says Baptist leader in new book", "url": "https://baptistnews.com/article/baptists-enough-respond-holocaust-complicated-says-baptist-leader-new-book/"}, {"title": "BAPTISTS, JEWS, AND THE HOLOCAUST", "url": "https://www.judsonpress.com/Products/J253/baptists-jews-and-the-holocaust.aspx"}, {"title": "Dr. Spitzer — Baptist Holocaust Studies", "url": "https://www.baptistholocauststudies.org/about"}, {"title": "Lee B. Spitzer — Judson Press", "url": "https://new.judsonpress.com/jp-3/lee-b-spitzer"}, {"title": "Christian Citizen Publishes Holocaust Article — Baptist Holocaust Studies", "url": "https://www.baptistholocauststudies.org/news/2017/10/24/christian-citizen-publishes-holocaust-article"}]}, "Lee B. Spitzer's PhD was in **theology**, not church history, and it came from Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam.\n\n- **Degree and school:** Baptist Holocaust Studies says that in September 2016, he was awarded a PhD degree in Theology for his work on Baptists and the Holocaust from Vrije University (Free University) Amsterdam, in association with the International Baptist Study Centre. An Amazon listing for his later book describes the same doctorate as coming in association with the International Baptist Theological Study Centre (IBTS).\n- **Current roles:** Judson Press describes him as Historian for the Baptist World Alliance and Affiliate Professor of Church History at Northern Seminary in Chicago. So the church history connection is through his teaching post, not his doctorate. The same page says he is the retired General Secretary of the American Baptist Churches USA.\n- **Book bio:** The Google Books listing for the 2017 book gives an older bio, saying he is Executive Minister of American Baptist Churches of New Jersey. That role is outdated.\n- **Personal background:** Baptist News reports that Spitzer, born into a Jewish home in Brooklyn, N.Y., converted to the Christian faith at age 14."], "durationSeconds": 5.595438707999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_011QCNaBd8t592eRfYDDnotK", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
